course: dictionary
lesson: 7441
title: What is a polymer?
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: A polymer is a substance made of very long chains. The word comes from two parts: «poly» means many and «mer» means part. So a polymer is many parts joined into one long chain.
explain: Each small part is called a monomer. Think of thousands of paperclips clipped into one chain: each paperclip is a small unit, and the whole chain is the polymer. «Plastics are polymers: very long chain molecules made by linking many small molecules together.»
explain: Polymers are not only plastic. Rubber is a natural polymer from the sap of rubber trees. Its chains are linked so that rubber springs back into shape after it has been stretched.
fact: A polymer is a substance made of very long chain-like molecules.
fact: The small units that join together to make a polymer are called monomers.
fact: «Poly» means many, and «mer» means part.
fact: Plastics are polymers, but so are natural things such as rubber, wool, silk, starch and the DNA in our cells.
fact: Polymer banknotes in Australia, Canada, the UK and New Zealand are made of a plastic polymer, not paper.
exercise: «Plastics are polymers: very long chain molecules made by linking many small molecules together.» What is a polymer? | A kind of metal that conducts electricity | A type of paper used for banknotes | A small molecule that cannot be joined to anything | *A substance made of very long chains of small units joined together
exercise: In the word polymer, what does «poly» mean? | Long | *Many | One | Plastic
exercise: Which of these is a natural polymer? | *Rubber from the sap of rubber trees | Salt from the sea | Glass from a window | Iron from a nail
test: «Rubber is a natural polymer from the sap of rubber trees; its chains are joined by links that pull it back into shape after stretching.» What does this tell you about rubber? | It is always see-through | *It springs back into shape after being stretched | It melts in hot water | It is made of paper
test: What are the small units called that join together to make a polymer? | Banknotes | Plastics | Paperclips | *Monomers
exam: Which of these is a natural polymer, and not a plastic? | A metal spoon | A rock from the beach | *Wool from a sheep | A glass bottle
